format session-log-v1
stamp 20260828.162148
editor Claude Code Terminal
provider Anthropic
product Claude Code
role HUSH -- Dream's planet, the hands-on systems half: Pond and the adaptation grant
modality text
model claude-opus-5
model_status active runtime unverified -- .claude/settings.json configures claude-opus-5 at max, which is configuration rather than telemetry
voice Kyri
host Framework laptop, NixOS, Linux 6.18 -- Eastern (EDT) one-clock
title the nib that outran its parent -- %322 booked and closed, the pin riding in a work commit as its own guard asks
prompt Continuing the same seat. The %321 round had landed on both remotes; re-reading the nib guards after the last rebase found one of them red.
think The mechanism, plainly: tools/r/remember_git_nib_witness.rish accepts a card nib naming HEAD, HEAD's pre-amend sibling, or HEAD's parent. The %321 round wrote 7071903c1b when that was its parent, then rebased twice as the twice-pulled rota asks, and a rebase gives a commit a new parent while the card inside the commit keeps naming the old one. The hash stayed real and pushed the whole time, so nib_honesty stayed green and remember_git_nib read stale -- the pair separating "is this hash honest" from "is this hash still this round's parent", which is the distinction the two guards exist to keep apart.
think I checked the guards again AFTER the final rebase rather than trusting the green I had taken before it. That is the whole of the catch, and it generalizes past nibs: a reading taken before a rebase describes a commit that no longer exists in that shape.
think The repair had one door. Amending is out -- the commit is pushed and force is forbidden. A pin-only follow-up is out too, and refused by name in the guard's own failure message: pin it in the NEXT work commit, never a pin-only follow-up. Booking the red IS work, so this commit carries the row that explains the fault and the pin that fixes it, which is what the tidy rule seated 20260728.205029 asks for.
obs Booked %322 from the anointed spine after a fetch, with xy/main equal to HEAD, so no collision this time -- unlike the round before it, where I booked %316 and upstream published its own %316 at stamp 20260828.143915 while I verified.
obs The rate is the finding underneath the finding. Fifteen commits landed on the anointed remote inside one twenty-five-minute roster run today. A round that writes its nib at the first rebase and verifies for half an hour will have the wrong parent by the time it pushes, every time. The nib belongs at the LAST rebase, and the guards belong after it.
loom guard=remember_git_nib before_rebases=green after_rebases=red nib_written=7071903c1b parent_after=d3ce030b41 repaired_to=8f5e83d6a3
loom guard=nib_honesty verdict=green throughout=yes pair_behaved=as_designed
loom reds_rows=322 booked=322 collision=none upstream_commits_per_roster_window=15
file construction/REDS.md %322 booked and closed -- a rebase moves the parent the nib names
file construction/ITINERARY.md the nib names 8f5e83d6a3, the parent this commit is made against
recommend keep-going -- Pond orbit two drives the enclosure declarations through Caravan's capability and address-space pieces, and the three bus doors of Bar 6 want declarations of their own. Two for Keaton, both standing: whether a one-page ITINERARY can hold six always-on lanes at six bytes of headroom, and the Constel predicate seat.
